  "pet_notes": "Adult compact boar yaoguai, 4 to 4.25 heads tall, short powerful legs, low center of gravity and round belly. Cuteness comes only from compact proportions, short muzzle, rounded cheeks and lively normal-sized reddish-brown eyes; never pink skin, baby proportions, blush, huge eyes, plush fur or bear/wolf face. Coarse grey-brown to smoke-brown bristles, dark wedge ears, broad textured black snout, two short upward tusks. Distressed low-saturation blue-green robe, narrow ochre trim, dark charcoal scarf, black bead strand, dark rope waist with bone clasp, layered dark split apron. Exactly one complete nine-toothed rake: full long wrapped shaft, visible bottom tail ferrule, aged bronze carved crossbar, exactly nine separated evenly spaced countable curved ivory teeth. No crop, no broken handle, no second rake head, no spear, fork, garden rake or crown. Canonical three-quarter near-front view with both hooves, belly and full rake inside frame.",
